# Optional. The usual way is to enter the Cato account ID and API key in the sandbox under Admin › Settings › Cato API
# (kept in the sandbox's data volume, encrypted). This file is the app.env-style alternative: copy it to
# ~/.config/licence-reporting/sandbox.env (outside the repo), fill in, and `chmod 600` it. run.sh mounts it read-only;
# it is never copied into the image. Without either, the sandbox runs with a made-up Cato group.
CATO_ACCOUNT_ID=
CATO_API_KEY=
# CATO_API_URL=https://api.catonetworks.com/api/v1/graphql2
